+# @deepseek-ai/dsh-vision-bridge
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+A default-enabled visual sub-agent bridge for text-only main models. DSH stores each uploaded image through the existing attachment service, materializes a stable extension-bearing read-only view scoped to the owning session, persists one adjacent `<system-reminder>` for every new image-bearing human message, and exposes `vision_inspect` so the main model can delegate a complete visual question to an administrator-configured OpenAI-compatible vision model. The main model never receives image tokens: DSH's text-only projection replaces every image block with a stable text handle, while the durable reminder carries the full current-session `attachment_id` and `local_path`.
+
+The bridge is enabled in the base bundle. Leave it enabled for native multimodal routes; those routes continue using DSH's native image path without this reminder or tool.
+
+## Configuration
+
+The base-bundle row is enabled by default. A deployment may restate the complete config when it needs to override the local defaults:
+
+```yaml
+- id: vision-bridge
+  disabled: false
+  config:
+    baseURL: !!js process.env.DSH_VISION_BASE_URL ?? 'https://ai.chuansgu.top/v1'
+    apiKeyEnv: QWEN_VISION_API_KEY
+    model: Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8
+    timeoutMs: 120000
+    maxImagesPerCall: 20
+    maxOutputTokens: 4096
+```
+
+`baseURL` falls back to the local DSH deployment endpoint and `/chat/completions` is appended unless it is already present. `apiKeyEnv` is a credential reference, resolved per call through `ctx.credentials` or the immutable launch environment. A literal `apiKey` is supported for controlled embedding but should not be committed. The numeric bounds fail loud unless they are positive integers.
+
+Loading the row is the enablement decision. It supplies the optional `imageInputBridge` admission capability, registers `vision_inspect`, and installs the durable reminder hook. There is no model preset or global prompt mutation.
+
+The package's browser half registers a dedicated `vision_inspect` Tool row at the same enablement boundary. It uses a compact eye icon and `Look` title instead of the generic Tool call label. The running row deliberately reads `Look ing <elapsed>` with a small visual gap between the title and activity suffix; the settled row reads `Look <duration>`. Because this keyed view owns its Think-shaped inline duration, it suppresses the generic trailing Tool duration. The row defines no private sweep and receives the one native in-flight sweep owned by the surrounding Tool call seat. The OpenAI-compatible request uses SSE and appends each visual-model Markdown fragment as a replayable `tool/progress` event keyed by the durable call id. While streaming, the one-line viewport follows the latest non-empty Markdown line and its newest text, then returns to the result's first line when settled. The final Markdown value lands once in the paired `tool/result`, and the disclosure retains the exact durable input and output. Progress is log-only and never enters model history, so it does not duplicate the result or change the request prefix. When the bridge is disabled, this keyed presentation is absent and the package exposes no visual Tool UI.
+
+## Durable history and KV cache
+
+The reminder is generated only while a newly claimed human message contains image blocks. Before insertion, the attachment backend may publish a verified copy below `attachments/v1/session-view/<session-hash>/<content-id>.<ext>`. The copy never links to the canonical object, its path does not contain the user-supplied filename, and the local backend publishes it read-only. The reminder is then inserted immediately after the message and appended by the ordinary agent loop as another durable `user/message`. Later turns replay that exact event; the plugin does not remove, regenerate, move, or re-inject old reminders. Thus the prior conversation remains an append-only request prefix and can reuse the same KV-cache entries as ordinary text history. A backend that cannot materialize a path, or a failed publication, records `local_path: unavailable` without blocking the image turn; attachment-id inspection remains available.
+
+Compaction may replace an old visible range with a summary according to the deployment's normal policy. The attachment authorization check still examines the complete session event log, including shadowed events, but the summary must preserve any `attachment_id` the main model may need later.
+
+## Session isolation and gateway contract
+
+`vision_inspect` accepts current-session `attachmentIds`, local image `paths`, or both. Before reading bytes, it resolves every requested id from uploaded image blocks or prior `vision/image-import` records in the calling agent's own session event stream. An unknown or cross-session id rejects the complete batch before any attachment or filesystem read and before any gateway request.
+
+Local paths resolve relative to the session workspace through the mounted `ctx.fs` backend; absolute paths use the same backend rules. The bridge accepts PNG/JPEG/WebP/GIF regular files, admits the complete path batch through the native attachment service, and appends only the resulting normalized references as one log-only `vision/image-import` event. It never stores source paths or image bytes in the session log. The combined references are content-id deduplicated and bounded by `maxImagesPerCall`, so later calls in this session may use the returned attachment ids without rereading the source files.
+
+The gateway receives one OpenAI-compatible chat-completions request containing the main model's complete delegated prompt, a stable label for each authorized attachment, and its data URL. The visual model is instructed to return concise task-directed Markdown: answer first, then visible evidence and necessary limitations. DSH preserves that Markdown without JSON parsing or field rewriting. Endpoint, credential, remote model, timing, and internal error bodies remain outside the result.
+
+## Model Experience
+
+### Upload reminder
+
+#### What the model sees
+
+Each newly uploaded image message is followed by one durable notice containing full current-session `attachment_id`, media type, and session-scoped `local_path` values. No notice is added after a tool result.
+
+##### Reminder template
+
+```markdown
+<system-reminder>
+本条用户消息包含图片，已保存到当前对话：
+- attachment_id: <full attachment id>，name: <optional escaped name>，media_type: <image media type>，local_path: <session path or unavailable>
+可使用 local_path 配合现有工具做确定性文件或像素分析；需要视觉理解时调用 vision_inspect。
+</system-reminder>
+```
+
+#### Token effect
+
+One bounded text notice is added for each image-bearing human message; each image contributes one identifier/path line. Image bytes do not enter main-model history. Old notices remain ordinary durable history and are not generated again.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+Append-only: the new user message and notice extend the reusable request prefix. Subsequent turns replay the exact stored events without mutation or reordering.
+
+### vision_inspect tool
+
+#### What the model sees
+
+The model sees the `vision_inspect` tool with optional `attachmentIds`, optional `paths`, and a required complete delegated `prompt`. At least one image source is required. The concise descriptions are:
+
+##### Tool definition
+
+```markdown
+Tool: Inspect conversation attachments or local image files with the configured vision model.
+attachmentIds: Current-conversation attachment IDs to inspect.
+paths: Image file paths to import into this conversation and inspect.
+prompt: The complete visual question or inspection task.
+```
+
+#### Token effect
+
+The stable tool definition is present whenever the plugin is loaded. A path call additionally adds one model-invisible import record containing normalized attachment references. Each successful call adds one Markdown tool result; source image bytes and data URLs never enter model history and exist only in the separate vision-gateway request.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+The stable tool definition is part of the reusable request prefix. Each new tool call and result is appended normally, without rewriting earlier reminders or observations.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+- **Compaction depends on identifier-preserving summaries** — the attachment remains authorized from the full event log, but the main model cannot choose a shadowed image if its compact summary drops the full `attachment_id`.
+- **One configured visual backend** — routing among multiple vision models, health-based failover, and per-workspace overrides are deferred.
+- **OpenAI-compatible transport only** — provider-native upload APIs and server-side image caches are not implemented.
+- **No automatic visual call** — the main model decides whether the user's task needs pixels; the bridge does not invoke the vision backend merely because an image was uploaded.
+- **The bridge is enabled by default in this DSH composition** — native multimodal routes still own their native image path, and a deployment may disable the bridge only when it intentionally does not want the reminder/tool experience.
